{"path":"numeric/random/piecewise_constant_distribution/operator()","title":"std::piecewise_constant_distribution<RealType>::operator()","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::piecewise_constant_distribution&lt;RealType&gt;::</span>operator()","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric/random/piecewise_constant_distribution/operator()","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"Generates random numbers that are distributed according to the associated probability function. The entropy is acquired by calling g.operator().","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Generator <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>result_type operator<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> Generator<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> g <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Generator <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>result_type operator<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> Generator<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> g, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> param_type<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> params <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Generates random numbers that are distributed according to the associated probability function. The entropy is acquired by calling <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">g.<span class=\"me1\">operator</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>. \n</p><p>The first version uses the associated parameter set, the second version uses <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">params</span></code>. The associated parameter set is not modified.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> g\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> a uniform random bit generator object\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> params\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> distribution parameter set to use instead of the associated one\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par-hitem\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"> Type requirements\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par-req\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"> -<div class=\"spacer\"></div><code>Generator</code> must meet the requirements of <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/UniformRandomBitGenerator\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">UniformRandomBitGenerator</em></a>.\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>The generated random number.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Complexity\">Complexity</h3>\n<p>Amortized constant number of invocations of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">g.<span class=\"me1\">operator</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</p>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Complexity","id":"Complexity"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics library"},{"path":"numeric/random","title":"Pseudo-random number generation"},{"path":"numeric/random/piecewise_constant_distribution","title":"std::piecewise_constant_distribution"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::piecewise_constant_distribution<RealType>::operator()","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++11. Generates random numbers that are distributed according to the associated probability function."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"g, params"},{"label":"Return value","note":"The generated random number."},{"label":"Complexity","note":"Amortized constant number of invocations of g.operator()."}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":108,"codeBlockCount":0}
